WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.593
- Thank you so much, thank you, thank you.

00:00:04.763 --> 00:00:07.346
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.700
- My name's Brianna and
I'm a former pageant girl.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.610
- I'm Rebecca Margaret
and I'm a pageant girl.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.333
- Hi, I'm Jarry and I've
competed in one pageant.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.993
- My name is Emily and
I'm a former pageant girl.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.280
- I feel people would ask is
there a height requirement.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.980
- How expensive it is,
just really expensive.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.560
- Are pageant girls mean?

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.453
- Or like the weird stuff,
like flippers and butt glue.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.070
- For the most part it is something to do

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.350
with community service.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.390
- Who you are as a person.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.520
- Academic achievement.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.353
- Your beauty.

00:00:42.353 --> 00:00:43.550
- Sometimes swimsuit.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.180
- The way that you can present yourself.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.080
- Answer questions like what
would I do to save the world

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.673
and stuff like that.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.360
- Oh, that's a tough one.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.720
- I don't think that pageants
are intended to be sexist,

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.920
I think they're intended to be empowering

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.370
and show that beauty is not
just about physical beauty,

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.970
but also you are on a
stage and you are sometimes

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:04.950
being objectified.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.700
- If you look this way in a swimsuit

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.020
and the other girl
doesn't then unfortunately

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.780
you are more likely to win
just based on your looks.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.770
- I think pageants may
be a little bit sexist

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:17.350
in that they only recognize
a very narrow view of beauty,

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.040
but I don't think there's anything wrong

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.720
with the women that do do pageants

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.130
and recognize for themselves
that they are beautiful,

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.320
and that's okay to show.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.020
- The ones that I've
competed in have been mostly

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.610
about my community service
and about my education,

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.110
not about the way that I look.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.590
- I think beauty pageants boost
self-confidence if you win

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:38.070
and if you don't win then
you'll be comparing yourself

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.260
to the person who did.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.360
- It is a little bit hard to be surrounded

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.370
by gorgeous women and not feel like

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.600
there might be something
wrong with your face.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.433
I'm fine now.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.950
- I came in to beauty
pageants after being bullied

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.230
and it really helped me
grow my confidence back

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.653
and believe in myself again.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.960
- I always got first
runner ups so I don't know

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.940
if I can answer that correctly.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.610
- I guess you just have to
impress the panel of judges

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.380
on pretty much every single category.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.330
- It's all about your
package and who you are

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.760
and what you're selling the judges.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.960
- I would say 80% of a beauty pageant

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.840
is what you're wearing,
your walk, your hair,

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.640
your makeup, and the
other 20% is your answers

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.453
to the questions that they ask you.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.720
- They can be beneficial
depending on why you enter.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.860
If you're entering to gain self-confidence

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.510
or because you like to, you
know, dress up and have fun

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.870
then it can be beneficial to you,

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.700
but not if you're the kind of person who

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.370
will really have the self-esteem
hit if they don't win.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:36.730
- I won a lot of self-confidence
after winning that pageant

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.970
and also I won a scholarship.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:41.610
- The pageants taught me how
to do a really mean catwalk

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.853
so they can benefit you.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.240
- Oh, a pageant walk
has a lot of confidence,

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.860
you have to strut your
stuff, you have to be elegant

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.690
and poised and just look really graceful.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.240
- You are always supposed
to be facing the judges

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.640
and the audience, just
walk with confidence.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.480
- You're walking very balanced
and you have your shoulders

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.400
back and your chest high.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.120
- And just remember to relax your arms,

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.940
you don't want like T-Rex arms.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.000
Remember to make eye
contact with the judges,

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.955
show them that you're
confident and like super cute.

00:03:12.955 --> 00:03:15.538
(upbeat music)

